VLA fine-tuning shifts to an entry-exit pattern (L0--L1: 21--24 heads, L31: 18), with intermediate layers markedly lower (0--11 at L2--L30); ordering is stable across thresholds (30\%--70\%; Appendix~\ref{sec:threshold_sensitivity}).

\paragraph{Task-specific sharpening.}
A fourth condition (OpenVLA-7B further fine-tuned on LIBERO) reveals stage-dependent refinement: L1 entry routing remains stable (22/32 heads, $56.9\%$ text attention), but L31 exit re-engagement disappears entirely (0 vs.\ 18 heads) and mid-depth compresses further (L9--L16: 0--7 vs.\ 5--11 heads).
The trajectory from general VLA to task-specific training thus sharpens routing from entry-exit to entry-only.

\paragraph{Probe robustness corroborates the pattern.}

